{"content":[{"c":["BETH-HORON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Canaanite place-name perhaps meaning “the house of Hauron,” the god of the underworld. Beth-horon was a dual settlement 10 and 12 miles (16.1 and 19.3 kilometers) northwest of Jerusalem. Located on the boundary between the tribal territories of Ephraim and Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.16.3,5","r":"Josh.16.3,5","rawR":"Josh.16.3,5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.16.3,5","value":"Josh.16.3,5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 16:3, 5"},"), the twin settlements controlled the valley of Aijalon, one of the most important ancient routes between the Mediterranean coast and the interior hill country. The upper town controlled a strategic pass. Ephraim’s “Beth-horon with its pasture lands” was assigned to the Levite family of Kohath (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.22","r":"Josh.21.22","rawR":"Josh.21.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.22","value":"Josh.21.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.68","r":"1Chr.6.68","rawR":"1Chr.6.68","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.68","value":"1Chr.6.68"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:68"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Many armies marched through the Aijalon Valley. Amorites pursued by Joshua’s army fled past Beth-horon after being defeated at Gibeon on “the day the sun stood still” (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.10.1-14","r":"Josh.10.1-14","rawR":"Josh.10.1-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.10.1-14","value":"Josh.10.1-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 10:1-14"},"). A band of Philistines approached it to make war with Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.13.18","r":"1Sam.13.18","rawR":"1Sam.13.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.13.18","value":"1Sam.13.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 13:18"},"). The Egyptian army of Shishak passed by Beth-horon (according to his Karnak inscription). Syrian armies under Seron (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.3.13-24","r":"1Macc.3.13-24","rawR":"1Macc.3.13-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.3.13-24","value":"1Macc.3.13-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 3:13-24"},") and Nicanor (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.7.39-43","r":"1Macc.7.39-43","rawR":"1Macc.7.39-43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.7.39-43","value":"1Macc.7.39-43"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:39-43"},") were defeated by Judas Maccabeus at Beth-horon. The Romans under Cestius were nearly annihilated there by the Jews, according to Jewish historian Josephus."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Beth-horon was probably destroyed and rebuilt more than once. Sheerah, Beriah’s daughter and Ephraim’s granddaughter, is credited with building both lower and upper Beth-horon (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.24","r":"1Chr.7.24","rawR":"1Chr.7.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.24","value":"1Chr.7.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:24"},"). King Solomon fortified both Beth-horons after raids in the vicinity by an Egyptian pharaoh (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.9.15-17","r":"1Kgs.9.15-17","rawR":"1Kgs.9.15-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.9.15-17","value":"1Kgs.9.15-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 9:15-17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.8.5","r":"2Chr.8.5","rawR":"2Chr.8.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.8.5","value":"2Chr.8.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 8:5"},"). In the intertestamental period Beth-horon was fortified by the Syrian general Bacchides after a battle with Jonathan Maccabeus (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.9.50","r":"1Macc.9.50","rawR":"1Macc.9.50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.9.50","value":"1Macc.9.50"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 9:50"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BethHoron","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 16:3, 5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.16.3,5","rawQueryValue":"Josh.16.3,5","sourceRefExact":"Josh.16.3,5"},{"anchorText":"Jos 21:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.22","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.22","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:68","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.68","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.68","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.68"},{"anchorText":"Jos 10:1-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.10.1-14","rawQueryValue":"Josh.10.1-14","sourceRefExact":"Josh.10.1-14"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 13:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.13.18","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.13.18","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.13.18"},{"anchorText":"1 Macc 3:13-24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.3.13-24","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.3.13-24","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.3.13-24"},{"anchorText":"7:39-43","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.7.39-43","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.7.39-43","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.7.39-43"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.24","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.24","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 9:15-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.9.15-17","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.9.15-17","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.9.15-17"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 8:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.8.5","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.8.5","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.8.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Macc 9:50","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.9.50","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.9.50","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.9.50"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"db569112c029e6462df82a6496a47c441a93a126f96487de80a343c98abc9b7a","sourceItemName":"BethHoron","sourceItemOrder":256,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BethHoron","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Beth-Horon","title":"Beth-Horon","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}